# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide shows how to use PEC combined with SLC to mitigate gate noise with reduced shot overhead compared to vanilla PEC.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng gabay na ito kung paano gamitin ang PEC kasama ng SLC para bawasan ang gate noise nang may mas mababang shot overhead kumpara sa vanilla PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The workflow follows:\n"
"1. Specify a circuit and observable.\n"
"2. Compute noisy, unmitigated expectation values.\n"
"3. Compute forward and backward bounds on the bias.\n"
"4. Learn the entangling layers' noise by using qiskit-noise-learning.\n"
"5. Use the learned noise to merge the computed bounds into a local scales matrix.\n"
"6. Choose the desired bias bound based on the shot overhead-bias trade-off.\n"
"7. Prepare a PEC + SLC program, execute the program, and post-process.\n"
"8. Compare the mitigated expectation values and shot overhead.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ganito ang workflow:\n"
"1. Tukuyin ang isang circuit at observable.\n"
"2. Kalkulahin ang mga noisy, unmitigated na expectation value.\n"
"3. Kalkulahin ang forward at backward na mga bound sa bias.\n"
"4. Alamin ang noise ng mga entangling layer gamit ang qiskit-noise-learning.\n"
"5. Gamitin ang natutunang noise para pagsamahin ang mga kinalkulang bound sa isang local scales matrix.\n"
"6. Piliin ang nais na bias bound batay sa trade-off ng shot overhead at bias.\n"
"7. Maghanda ng PEC + SLC program, patakbuhin ang programa, at mag-post-process.\n"
"8. Ihambing ang mga mitigated na expectation value at shot overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
