# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute noisy, unmitigated expectation values {#compute-noisy-unmitigated-expectation-values}"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang mga noisy, unmitigated na expectation value {#compute-noisy-unmitigated-expectation-values}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs) contains a quantum circuit and a [samplex](/addons/samplomatic/guides/samplex-io) in a format suitable for the [Executor](/guides/get-started-with-executor) primitive. `MitigationTask.prepare` builds a `QuantumProgram` from the circuit, the observables and the parameter values, and boxes the circuit with the given boxing options. Set the ``measure_annotations`` boxing option to ``\"change_basis\"`` to rotate the measurements into the required bases, and add ``add_tags: \"unique_box\"`` so the simulator can map a noise model onto the circuit's boxes. The program is Pauli twirled by default, which on hardware turns coherent noise into the Pauli noise that the mitigation methods assume. `num_randomizations` sets how many twirled instances of each circuit are sampled and `shots_per_randomization` sets how many shots each instance receives, so their product is the shot limit per circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs) ay naglalaman ng isang quantum circuit at isang [samplex](/addons/samplomatic/guides/samplex-io) sa format na angkop para sa [Executor](/guides/get-started-with-executor) primitive. Binubuo ng `MitigationTask.prepare` ang isang `QuantumProgram` mula sa circuit, mga observable at mga parameter value, at ibinabox ang circuit gamit ang ibinigay na mga boxing option. Itakda ang boxing option na ``measure_annotations`` sa ``\"change_basis\"`` para i-rotate ang mga measurement sa kinakailangang mga basis, at idagdag ang ``add_tags: \"unique_box\"`` para maimapa ng simulator ang isang noise model sa mga box ng circuit. Pauli twirled ang programa bilang default, na sa hardware ay ginagawang Pauli noise ang coherent noise na ipinapalagay ng mga paraan ng mitigation. Itinatakda ng `num_randomizations` kung ilang twirled na instance ng bawat circuit ang sina-sample at itinatakda ng `shots_per_randomization` kung ilang shot ang natatanggap ng bawat instance, kaya ang kanilang produkto ang shot limit bawat circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you have QPU access, you can execute the program with an `Executor` built from a backend of the `QiskitRuntimeService`. This example uses an `AerSimulator` to run the program locally. Its `layer_noise_model` simulator option injects noise from a given Pauli-Lindblad noise model on every layer of entangling gates. Here we generate a random Pauli-Lindblad noise model with an error per layered gate (EPLG) of ``0.01``, almost an order of magnitude higher than typical current Heron QPUs, to magnify the effect of using SLC also on a small scale problem.\n"
msgstr "Kung may access ka sa QPU, maaari mong patakbuhin ang programa gamit ang `Executor` na binuo mula sa isang backend ng `QiskitRuntimeService`. Gumagamit ang halimbawang ito ng `AerSimulator` para patakbuhin ang programa nang lokal. Ang simulator option nitong `layer_noise_model` ay nag-i-inject ng noise mula sa isang ibinigay na Pauli-Lindblad noise model sa bawat layer ng entangling gates. Dito, bumubuo tayo ng random na Pauli-Lindblad noise model na may error per layered gate (EPLG) na ``0.01``, halos isang order of magnitude na mas mataas kaysa sa tipikal na kasalukuyang Heron QPU, para palakihin ang epekto ng paggamit ng SLC kahit sa maliit na problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute forward and backward bounds on the bias {#compute-forward-and-backward-bounds-on-the-bias}"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang forward at backward na mga bound sa bias {#compute-forward-and-backward-bounds-on-the-bias}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before spending any QPU time on noise learning, SLC uses classical simulation to bound each potential error's contribution to the observable's bias. This is done in two complementary passes:\n"
msgstr "Bago gumugol ng anumang oras ng QPU sa noise learning, gumagamit ang SLC ng classical simulation para i-bound ang kontribusyon ng bawat posibleng error sa bias ng observable. Ginagawa ito sa dalawang magkatuwang na pass:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Forward propagation**: each Pauli error is propagated forward through the remainder of the circuit and its commutator with the observable is evaluated. An error that anti-commutes with the observable is the only kind that can bias the result, so this pass produces an upper bound on each error's forward impact.\n"
msgstr "**Forward propagation**: ipinapakalat pasulong ang bawat Pauli error sa natitirang bahagi ng circuit at sinusuri ang commutator nito sa observable. Ang error na anti-commute sa observable ang tanging uri na maaaring magdulot ng bias sa resulta, kaya nagbibigay ang pass na ito ng upper bound sa forward impact ng bawat error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Backward propagation**: each error is propagated backward to the start of the circuit and its commutator with the initial state is evaluated. Because the circuit starts in the all-zero state, errors that commute with it cannot affect the outcome, tightening the bound from the other direction.\n"
msgstr "**Backward propagation**: ipinapakalat paurong ang bawat error hanggang sa simula ng circuit at sinusuri ang commutator nito sa initial state. Dahil nagsisimula ang circuit sa all-zero state, ang mga error na nag-commute rito ay hindi makakaapekto sa kalalabasan, kaya humihigpit ang bound mula sa kabilang direksyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two bounds together form a tight bracket around every error's worst-case contribution to the bias. In the next step these bounds are merged with the learned noise rates to rank which errors are worth correcting and which can be safely left alone. The `inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"` boxing option is required here so that each `InjectNoise` annotation in the boxed circuit has a unique identity that the SLC bounds can be attached to.\n"
msgstr "Magkasamang bumubuo ang dalawang bound ng mahigpit na bracket sa paligid ng worst-case na kontribusyon ng bawat error sa bias. Sa susunod na hakbang, pinagsasama ang mga bound na ito sa mga natutunang noise rate para i-rank kung aling mga error ang sulit itama at alin ang ligtas na iwan. Kailangan dito ang boxing option na `inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"` para ang bawat `InjectNoise` annotation sa naka-box na circuit ay may natatanging identity kung saan maiuugnay ang mga SLC bound.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For larger-scale problems, these computations may demand substantial classical computational resources.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mas malalaking problema, maaaring mangailangan ang mga kalkulasyong ito ng malaking classical na computational resource.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the entangling layers' noise {#learn-the-entangling-layers-noise}"
msgstr "Alamin ang noise ng mga entangling layer {#learn-the-entangling-layers-noise}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In order to compute a final estimation of how much each error impacts on the expectation value's bias, as well as how expensive it would be to correct it, we learn the noise rates and apply them to the predicted noise bounds we computed before.\n"
msgstr "Para makalkula ang pinal na pagtantiya kung gaano naaapektuhan ng bawat error ang bias ng expectation value, pati kung gaano kamahal itong itama, inaalam natin ang mga noise rate at inilalapat ang mga ito sa mga tinatayang noise bound na kinalkula natin kanina.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC (as well as PEC+SLC) assumes a twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit. If you assume a Markovian noise model, the depth of the circuit is assumed to not affect the noise channel of a given entangling layer. Therefore, only the noise model of each unique layer of entangling gates should be learned. The circuit used in this guide can be split into two unique layers. Designing circuits to have a minimal set of unique entangling layers is important if you want to learn a noise model, since the unique layers must be learned independently. If you have too many unique layers in your circuit, noise learning can become infeasible due to the sampling cost of learning many layers.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapalagay ng PEC (pati ng PEC+SLC) ang twirled na noise model ng bawat layer ng entangling gates sa circuit. Kung ipinapalagay mo ang Markovian na noise model, ipinapalagay na hindi naaapektuhan ng depth ng circuit ang noise channel ng isang entangling layer. Kaya, ang noise model lang ng bawat natatanging layer ng entangling gates ang kailangang matutunan. Ang circuit na ginamit sa gabay na ito ay maaaring hatiin sa dalawang natatanging layer. Mahalagang idisenyo ang mga circuit na may pinakamaliit na set ng natatanging entangling layer kung gusto mong matutunan ang isang noise model, dahil kailangang matutunan nang hiwalay ang mga natatanging layer. Kung masyadong marami ang natatanging layer sa circuit mo, maaaring maging imposible ang noise learning dahil sa sampling cost ng pag-aaral ng maraming layer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit-noise-learning` is used to learn the noise. The learner repeats each layer _`fragment_depths`_ times in its learning circuits, twirls each circuit _`num_randomizations`_ times, and fits the decay of the measured fidelities to a Pauli-Lindblad model. These parameters can affect the accuracy of the learned model. The more accurate the learned noise model is, the more accurate the noise cancellation will be.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ang `qiskit-noise-learning` para matutunan ang noise. Inuulit ng learner ang bawat layer nang _`fragment_depths`_ beses sa mga learning circuit nito, nagta-twirl ng bawat circuit nang _`num_randomizations`_ beses, at ifi-fit ang pagbaba ng mga nasukat na fidelity sa isang Pauli-Lindblad model. Maaaring makaapekto ang mga parameter na ito sa katumpakan ng natutunang model. Kung mas tumpak ang natutunang noise model, mas tumpak din ang pagkansela ng noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code draws the learned noise model with the two layers merged into one map. Each qubit is a pie of its weight-1 X, Y and Z rates summed over the two layers, and each edge shows the learned weight-2 rates. For example, a rate of ``3e-4`` means that error occurs on roughly three of every 10,000 uses of the layer.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na code ang natutunang noise model kung saan pinagsama sa isang mapa ang dalawang layer. Ang bawat qubit ay isang pie ng weight-1 na X, Y at Z rate nito na pinagsama sa dalawang layer, at ipinapakita ng bawat edge ang mga natutunang weight-2 rate. Halimbawa, ang rate na ``3e-4`` ay nangangahulugang nagaganap ang error na iyon sa humigit-kumulang tatlo sa bawat 10,000 gamit ng layer.\n"

